# Rank 1740 / CVE-2022-23837: Sidekiq's Web UI dashboard passed the `days`
# query parameter straight into the stats-history window. `params["days"]` is
# request input, and Ruby's `to_i` never raises -- `"1000000"` coerces to a
# million, garbage to 0 -- so `Sidekiq::Stats::History.new((params["days"] ||
# 30).to_i)` handed the peer an unbounded window count, and `date_stat_hash`
# iterated `@start_date.downto(@start_date - @days_previous + 1)`, building a
# date-keyed array and one Redis MGET of that size per request (CWE-400 DoS in
# the Web UI). Fix 7785ac13 bounds the window twice: the route validates
# `days < 1 || days > 180` and halts 401, and `History#initialize` raises
# ArgumentError outside 1..(5*365). The parent 0a4de94 is vulnerable and the
# remediation is present at the fixed revision, so the row is sound.
#
# ATTENTION, two independent blockers, both measured.
#
# 1. No iteration-count sink vocabulary exists in any language, so even the
# one-function form reports nothing today. A throwaway in-tree sink on
# `downto`/`upto` args[0] emitting a consumed sink concept makes
# VYQL-INJ-002 report the one-function form below (`params["days"].to_i`
# flows through the `|| 30` default, the assignment and the arithmetic into
# the loop argument -- `vyql match` labels `params` and `params.__subscript`
# as code.HttpInput, `ruby.input`), proving the source half and the taint
# half work and isolating the missing half to the sink. Emitting the sink as
# code.UnboundedResourceOperation does not compile: the corpus validator
# rejects `emit sink` on a concept of kind issue, and VYQL-DOS-042's rule is
# presence-shaped (`issue ... as sink`), so riding it from a taint path would
# need a new sink-kind concept plus a consuming `taint core.UserControlledData
# -> ...` rule, and that is a minted rule whose precision has not been
# measured here. A route-level presence binding is unshippable instead:
# `params[...].to_i` occurs 107 times across the other cloned trees
# (mastodon, redmine, open-build-service, rails -- the pagination idiom), all
# without a halt, and keying the consumer (`Stats.History.new`) fails the
# rename test and names the incident rather than the API. Same family as the
# measured-unshippable CWE-400 shapes (1517, 1534, 1554, 1559, 1572, 1586,
# 1612, and 1355's 1 -> 124).
#
# 2. Even with a sink, the count never reaches the loop across the class
# boundary. Full `--cache off` scans of both revisions (three runs per side,
# stable): 64 findings at the parent, 64 at the fixed revision, nothing on
# web/application.rb:53 or api.rb:161-190 in either. `vyql trace` on the
# parent shows the HttpInput at application.rb:53 flowing through `to_i`,
# into `Sidekiq.Stats.History.new` and onto the `stats_history` receiver --
# then dead: `stats_history.processed` / `.failed` report "callee not traced
# -- external or cross-package" (cross-file receiver-typed dispatch through a
# local assigned from a namespaced constructor). From the callee side the
# `days_previous` parameter of History#initialize is itself labelled
# code.ExternalEntryInput (api.rb:163) and its taint stops at the very next
# statement: `@days_previous = days_previous` never flows to the `@days_previous`
# read inside date_stat_hash. A one-file collapse with the resolution present
# (below) reproduces the same dead end -- taint passes through `h.processed`
# into the caller's return but the callee body's loop argument stays clean --
# while the identical count through a plain method argument reports under the
# throwaway sink. So the engine is missing two relations: constructor-argument
# taint entering the resolved initialize body, and instance-variable
# write -> read across methods (the aliasReceiverSelf field-crossing family
# recorded for 1198/1287, here in Ruby form). Both are new dataflow
# relations, not localized corrections, so this is not a mechanical fix.
#
# Spec cve_rank1740 pins all four directions against VYQL-DOS-042, the rule
# of the right weakness class that exists today. When iteration-count sink
# vocabulary lands, the one-function member must flip to expect; when the
# constructor-argument -> instance-variable hop lands, the same-file member
# must flip too; when cross-file receiver resolution lands, the two-file
# member follows. The patched member must stay reject under all of them.

test "rank1740: the dashboard passes the unvalidated days parameter straight into the stats history window"
  lang ruby
  file sidekiq/web/application.rb
  reject VYQL-DOS-042
  code
  ```
  module Sidekiq
    class WebApplication
      get "/" do
        @redis_info = redis_info.select { |k, v| REDIS_KEYS.include? k }
        stats_history = Sidekiq::Stats::History.new((params["days"] || 30).to_i)
        @processed_history = stats_history.processed
        @failed_history = stats_history.failed

        erb(:dashboard)
      end
    end
  end
  ```
  file sidekiq/api.rb
  code
  ```
  module Sidekiq
    module Stats
      class History
        def initialize(days_previous, start_date = nil)
          @days_previous = days_previous
          @start_date = start_date || Time.now.utc.to_date
        end

        def processed
          @processed ||= date_stat_hash("processed")
        end

        def failed
          @failed ||= date_stat_hash("failed")
        end

        private

        def date_stat_hash(stat)
          stat_hash = {}
          dates = @start_date.downto(@start_date - @days_previous + 1).map { |date|
            date.strftime("%Y-%m-%d")
          }

          keys = dates.map { |datestr| "stat:#{stat}:#{datestr}" }

          Sidekiq.redis do |conn|
            conn.mget(keys).each_with_index do |value, idx|
              stat_hash[dates[idx]] = value ? value.to_i : 0
            end
          end

          stat_hash
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1740: the fixed revision bounds the window at the route and raises in the constructor"
  lang ruby
  file sidekiq/web/application.rb
  reject VYQL-DOS-042
  code
  ```
  module Sidekiq
    class WebApplication
      get "/" do
        @redis_info = redis_info.select { |k, v| REDIS_KEYS.include? k }
        days = (params["days"] || 30).to_i
        return halt(401) if days < 1 || days > 180

        stats_history = Sidekiq::Stats::History.new(days)
        @processed_history = stats_history.processed
        @failed_history = stats_history.failed

        erb(:dashboard)
      end
    end
  end
  ```
  file sidekiq/api.rb
  code
  ```
  module Sidekiq
    module Stats
      class History
        def initialize(days_previous, start_date = nil)
          # we only store five years of data in Redis
          raise ArgumentError if days_previous < 1 || days_previous > (5 * 365)
          @days_previous = days_previous
          @start_date = start_date || Time.now.utc.to_date
        end

        def processed
          @processed ||= date_stat_hash("processed")
        end

        def failed
          @failed ||= date_stat_hash("failed")
        end

        private

        def date_stat_hash(stat)
          stat_hash = {}
          dates = @start_date.downto(@start_date - @days_previous + 1).map { |date|
            date.strftime("%Y-%m-%d")
          }

          keys = dates.map { |datestr| "stat:#{stat}:#{datestr}" }

          Sidekiq.redis do |conn|
            conn.mget(keys).each_with_index do |value, idx|
              stat_hash[dates[idx]] = value ? value.to_i : 0
            end
          end

          stat_hash
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1740: the same count inline in one function is the shape a sink can reach"
  lang ruby
  file inline_history.rb
  reject VYQL-DOS-042
  code
  ```
  def history_keys(days)
    today = Time.now.utc.to_date
    dates = today.downto(today - days + 1).map { |date| date.strftime("%Y-%m-%d") }
    dates.map { |datestr| "stat:processed:#{datestr}" }
  end

  get "/export" do
    days = (params["days"] || 30).to_i
    history_keys(days)
  end
  ```

test "rank1740: the count crossing a constructor into an instance variable keeps the loop bound unreachable"
  lang ruby
  file same_file_history.rb
  reject VYQL-DOS-042
  code
  ```
  module Sidekiq
    module Stats
      class History
        def initialize(days_previous, start_date = nil)
          @days_previous = days_previous
          @start_date = start_date || Time.now.utc.to_date
        end

        def processed
          @processed ||= date_stat_hash("processed")
        end

        private

        def date_stat_hash(stat)
          dates = @start_date.downto(@start_date - @days_previous + 1).map { |date|
            date.strftime("%Y-%m-%d")
          }
          dates.map { |datestr| "stat:#{stat}:#{datestr}" }
        end
      end
    end
  end

  def dashboard
    stats_history = Sidekiq::Stats::History.new((params["days"] || 30).to_i)
    @processed_history = stats_history.processed
  end
  ```
